osed labels (icons, checkboxes), provide `textValue` to `MenuItem` for typeahead search."],[850,"**Typed Refs:** Refs are correctly typed based on the `as` value - `useRef<HTMLButtonElement>` works with `as=\"button\"`."],[222,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[684,"**TypeScript support**: Fully typed with comprehensive prop interfaces"],[890,"**Use `Grid` when**: You need explicit two-dimensional layouts with rows and columns, named grid areas, or responsive auto-fill patterns."],[751,"**Use default mode** for SSR applications or when icons appear infrequently"],[752,"**Use sprite mode** when the same icons appear many times (navigation, lists, tables)"],[762,"**Use sprite mode**: For repeated icons, consider sprite mode which consolidates multiple icons into a single SVG sprite sheet, reducing DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1020,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1333,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1546,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1018,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[271,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[214,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[247,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[223,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[738,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[153,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[846,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[622,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1189,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1310,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[465,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[377,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1190,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1311,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[379,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1192,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1642,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1312,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[464,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[378,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1191,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[462,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[461,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[463,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[838,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[855,"`BoxContext` supplies default props to Boxes in its subtree. A `slots` map supplies defaults to\nnamed parts; each Box selects one with `slot`. Explicit consumer props override defaults, while\nclasses, styles, and refs are merged. Pass `slot={null}` to opt out of the context."],[502,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[152,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[183,"`CardGroup` uses grid navigation: Tab enters or leaves, arrow keys move between Cards, and Space\nchanges selection. Enter activates row actions or links. Choose selection or `onAction`;\ncombining them prevents pointer selection."],[363,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[424,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[436,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[420,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[429,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1682,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[130,"`CloseButton` dismisses an overlay: it defaults to `slot=\"close\"` and renders an `x` icon labelled \"Close\"."],[497,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[503,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[504,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[499,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[546,"`commitBehavior` on `DateRangePickerCalendar` applies to both presentations."],[1138,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[713,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[716,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[712,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[714,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[715,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[717,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1437,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[1367,"`default`, `full`, and `none` rounding"],[544,"`drawerProps` customizes the drawer, which defaults to `85dvh`; `popoverProps` customizes the popover."],[564,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[634,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1601,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[621,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[867,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[721,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[889,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid